Some enumerated neighbourhood is contained in the intersection of two enumerated neighbourhoods if and only if the intersection code of the indices truncated at 2 is different from 3.

Rewrite the intersection by the intersection-code formula. If a value of the enumeration is contained in the intersection and the code equals 3, the intersection is empty, so that value is empty. If the code is different from 3, the intersection equals the neighbourhood enumerated by the code, which contains itself.
